WEBVTT

NOTE Made by video/captions.py from the voice lines in video/vo.py.

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.777
Marginborn keeps the passages you read, and the thoughts they start. Here is how it works.

00:00:07.277 --> 00:00:13.410
It all starts from five places on the bottom bar: Home, Commonplace, Capture, Search, and Profile.

00:00:15.977 --> 00:00:17.597
Chapter one. Getting in.

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:22.917
Sign in with an email code, or with Google.

00:00:22.917 --> 00:00:27.831
A new account then sets up encryption, so your notes are encrypted before they leave the phone.

00:00:31.172 --> 00:00:33.682
The app locks when Android closes it.

00:00:33.682 --> 00:00:37.062
Unlock with your passkey, or later with your fingerprint.

00:00:37.062 --> 00:00:40.528
To add a second device, make a one-time code in Settings.

00:00:43.758 --> 00:00:45.333
Chapter two. Capturing.

00:00:47.258 --> 00:00:49.898
Tap Capture to photograph a passage.

00:00:49.898 --> 00:00:55.104
Marginborn reads what you marked, and the text appears with its source and suggested ideas.

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:02.787
Ideas come by themselves after a photo.

00:01:02.787 --> 00:01:08.642
Marginborn also checks a photo's text for details like card numbers or email addresses.

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:14.430
You can share a passage, a link, or a picture from another app.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:17.575
Marginborn opens it as a form, ready to review.

00:01:21.806 --> 00:01:23.633
Chapter three. Your Commonplace.

00:01:25.306 --> 00:01:30.194
Your Commonplace shows the same notes two ways: as a cloud of ideas, or as a list.

00:01:37.001 --> 00:01:40.791
Open a note to see its source, its ideas, and its margins.

00:01:40.791 --> 00:01:43.252
Hold a card to edit, share, or delete it.

00:01:47.682 --> 00:01:49.659
Chapter four. Following a thought.

00:01:51.182 --> 00:01:53.572
Every note is filed under ideas.

00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:56.970
See Related Notes opens The Stem: the notes that share them.

00:02:04.306 --> 00:02:09.286
The Lexicon keeps what you make: your own ideas, collections, lenses, and questions.

00:02:16.953 --> 00:02:20.303
Check-ins ask whether your questions are still open.

00:02:20.303 --> 00:02:24.651
And when many notes have no ideas, Marginborn offers to tag them for you.

00:02:26.444 --> 00:02:28.376
Chapter five. Finding things.

00:02:29.944 --> 00:02:32.594
Search finds notes by word as you type.

00:02:32.594 --> 00:02:35.749
Press Search to find notes by meaning, right on your phone.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.719
The Library keeps your books on three shelves.

00:02:45.719 --> 00:02:48.705
Duplicates are found for you, but only you merge them.

00:02:54.463 --> 00:02:56.360
Chapter six. Looking after it.

00:02:57.963 --> 00:03:03.228
In Settings, choose light or dark. Screenshots of notes stay blank unless you allow them.

00:03:05.848 --> 00:03:11.977
You can export a backup, import from Readwise, and sign out to remove Marginborn's data from the phone.

00:03:16.115 --> 00:03:20.465
Your note and question text is encrypted with your key before it syncs.

00:03:20.465 --> 00:03:27.835
Photos and text sent to be read go through Marginborn's server, and are never used for training or advertising.

00:03:27.835 --> 00:03:29.981
Search by meaning stays on the phone.

00:03:34.115 --> 00:03:35.775
Build your Commonplace.

00:03:35.775 --> 00:03:41.455
Marginborn is in testing, and Android testers can join now, at marginborn.com.
